casmi26 — third-party material

1. prvsiyan, "Analog Propagation CASMI 2026 baseline" (Kaggle notebook,
   kaggle.com/code/prvsiyan/analog-propagation-casmi-2026-baseline), Apache License 2.0.
   - src/casmi/fpmodel.py adapts its FPNet architecture (SinEmb, Block, FPNet) and its
     input preparation (prep_peaks, peak merging, adduct / instrument vocabularies) so
     that the published checkpoints below load unchanged.
   - scripts/fork_prvsiyan.py rebuilds its scored V33 cell, unmodified, as a private kernel.
   - src/casmi/rank31.py ports its candidate ranking features (rank_features), its MetFrag-lite
     fragmentation score and its ranker recipe (HistGradientBoosting, class weights, seeds).

2. prvsiyan/casmi26-fp-models-v2 (Kaggle dataset; fp_single_s2.pt, fp_merged_m1.pt) and
   fp_bits.npy from prvsiyan/coconut-casmi26-candidates, Creative Commons
   Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0).
   Used as attached Kaggle inputs and local downloads under external/ for a leaderboard
   test of the fingerprint channel. They are not redistributed in this repository or in
   our datasets, and no adapted checkpoint is published. Their licence is not Apache 2.0:
   the non-commercial and share-alike terms apply to any further use.

   prvsiyan/casmi26-ranker-features (rank_train.npz) is CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 as well. None of the
   CC BY-NC-SA material enters a final submission; it is used for leaderboard comparisons only.

3. prvsiyan/pubchem-npformula-massindex and prvsiyan/pubchem-popularity-counts (Kaggle
   datasets, CC0 1.0), built from NCBI PubChem (public domain).

4. COCONUT 2.0 natural products (coconut.naturalproducts.net), CC0 1.0.

5. Competition data: Enveda CASMI 2026 (Kaggle), under the competition's data licence.

6. coleygroup/ms-pred (github.com/coleygroup/ms-pred, commit 708148c2), MIT License,
   Copyright (c) 2023 Samuel Goldman.
   - src/casmi/forward/glacier.py and src/casmi/forward/iceberg.py re-implement the inference
     paths of GLACIER and ICEBERG 2.1 in plain PyTorch (no code of the repository is executed).
   - The Graphormer encoder in glacier.py follows ms-pred's graphormer/ files: MIT License,
     Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation; parts Copyright (c) Facebook, Inc. and its affiliates.
   - GatedGraphConv in iceberg.py comes from DGL (as copied into ms-pred's nn_utils/dgl_modules.py),
     Apache License 2.0.
   - Weights: red6161/casmi26-forward-msg holds weights-only copies of the public MassSpecGym
     checkpoints (ICEBERG msg_all, GLACIER msg) linked from the ms-pred README; MassSpecGym
     (huggingface.co/datasets/roman-bushuiev/MassSpecGym) is MIT. No NIST-trained weights.

